  "notes": [
    "Regional site overlay (ADR 0042) for the rebel kings' camp during the siege of Reval, May 1343: a forest clearing by the Pirita, the four elected kings' shelters and council fire inside a stake fence, groups of low shelters with cooking fires outside it, a field smithy, the horse lines on a wet meadow and the tracks to the Harju villages and south toward Kanavere.",
    "Invented composite (docs/LOCATIONS/rebel_kings_camp.md, history/dossiers/hinterland/harju-rebel-camp-and-pirita-approach-1343.md): no source places the camp. The terrain is EU-DEM in the Pirita valley at Vaskjala (Rae parish), a representative forested reach of the eastern Harju corridor about 12 km from Reval, chosen for the game; it is not the signal hill and claims nothing about Vaskjala. Coordinates are metres from that origin, x east, y south.",
    "The river course is the OSM Pirita joegi (way 79505481), simplified; the modern reservoir, village, fields and ditches are not used. Points of interest of kind campfire carry the fire size for the site script (scenes/world/sites/hinterland_site.gd).",
    "Shelters are low pole-and-bough huts drawn as thatched outbuildings (no chimneys, no windows); the stake fence is the pipeline's palisade circuit with two wooden gates."
  ],
